# Vendra is cloud-only: it always boots against Supabase.
# Both vars are REQUIRED at build time. A build made without them renders an
# honest "cloud backend is not configured" screen instead of the app.
#
# Setup path (see README.md "First-run setup & master account"):
#   1. Create a free project at supabase.com -> Dashboard -> New project.
#   2. In the SQL editor run the supabase/migrations/ files in numeric
#      order (the set grows with releases; run ALL of them, in order).
#   3. Copy this project's URL and client key (Project Settings -> API):
#      - NEW projects: the "publishable key" (starts with sb_publishable_).
#        Fresh projects no longer have a JWT "anon key" — the publishable
#        key is the right one to paste here.
#      - OLDER projects: the legacy "anon key" (starts with eyJ…) still
#        works and is equally fine.
#      NEVER paste the "secret key" (sb_secret_…) or a service_role key
#      here. Those bypass all database security and must never ship inside
#      the app — the app refuses to boot with a secret key on purpose.
#   4. npm install && npm run build, then deploy dist/ to any static host.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://xyzcompany.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_...
